- op: discuss  # 29e5
  at: '2026-10-12T16:41:09Z'  # 29e5
  by: agent  # 29e5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 29e5
  clock: 3  # 29e5
  nonce: '29e5'  # 29e5
  message: "Fixed in PR #1556 (merge 9f400e64fc). Root cause: elixir.py only knew defmodule as a module definer, so defs under defprotocol/defimpl took the nearest defmodule (or none) as owner. Fix: defmodule/defprotocol/defimpl share _enclosing_module_names; defprotocol P -> module P with abstract callback-shaped heads (meta arity, callback_stable_id, qualified call targets); defimpl P, for: T -> absolute module P.T (for: [A,B] one per target, no for:/__MODULE__ -> enclosing module, P/T alias-expanded incl. nested-module auto-aliases; unreadable impls own nothing). Edges via _behaviour_edges/hypergumbo_core.behaviours: implements P.T->P (or external unresolved), protocol fn -> impl dispatches_to by name+arity; impls of non-repo protocols rooted by module->public fn dispatches_to. Gaps: @derive not modelled (generated impl, no source); calls in a multi-target impl anchor on one target's copy. Evidence: hypergumbo run on the filed repro (dev 9f400e64fc) -> modules Outer, Size, Size.Map, Size.Outer; functions Size.size [abstract], Size.Map.size, Size.Outer.size, all stable_ids non-null, no bare size; edges implements Size.Map->Size, Size.Outer->Size, dispatches_to Size.size->Size.Map.size, Size.size->Size.Outer.size. Corpus (analyzer level, before->after): bare protocol/impl fns plausible 23->0, livebook 335->0, phoenix 15->0, nex 4->0; impl public fns with no in-edge plausible 21->0, livebook 284->0, phoenix 15->0, nex 24->0; implements edges plausible 135->159, livebook 131->148, phoenix 95->103, nex 14->20."  # 29e5
